.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH maw-add 1  "maw-add " 
.SH NAME
maw\-add \- copy a file or dir into static/, then activate so it\*(Aqs linked back in place
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaw add\fR [\fB\-\-no\-activate\fR] [\fB\-\-secret\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
copy a file or dir into static/, then activate so it\*(Aqs linked back in place
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-activate\fR
only copy; activate later
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\fR
encrypt it into static/ instead, for every machine\*(Aqs key
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
file or dir to copy
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
registry name to file it under; inferred from the path when omitted
.SH EXTRA
see: maw help adding verbatim files
